- op: discuss  # 1cbd
  at: '2026-07-29T18:45:23Z'  # 1cbd
  by: agent  # 1cbd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1cbd
  clock: 4  # 1cbd
  nonce: 1cbd  # 1cbd
  message: "PRIORITY P1 + todo_hard (owner directive 2026-07-29: 'bump WI-sikar to P1 and do it next'), following the evidence in the preceding entry that the deferral rationale was backwards -- colon-bearing selector ids are ALREADY unparseable, so the fold fixes a live correctness gap rather than churning good values.\n\nSTALE RELEASE GATE CORRECTED. The description says the change 'must ride the v6 stable_id bump, NOT land pre-v6.' Written 2026-06-13; STABLE_ID_SCHEME is now hypergumbo-stableid-v8, so v6 shipped two bumps ago and the gate is discharged by time. Recording this explicitly because 'must ride a bump' is exactly what a future session reads as 'still blocked' (the same trap WI-banod T1 carries, register pt.33).\n\nNO COLLISION WITH THE WI-talos v9/v10 SEQUENCING. WI-sikar changes node.id (the ADR-0036 composite). v9's unqualified digest-compatibility claim is about the four *_scheme digests (stable_id / shape_id / repo_fingerprint / symbol_fingerprint). assemble_stable_id hashes the raw Symbol.name, not the sanitized id name-slot, so no digest moves and v9's claim stays true. Consistent with the scheme-bump principle (correctness pt.34): node.id is not a *_scheme field, and WI-zugob's route sweep changed node.id kind-slots fleet-wide last session with no bump and no release gate. To be re-verified empirically before relying on it."  # 1cbd
